          "text": "The user is asking about DLL search order on Windows. This is a factual question about how Windows locates DLLs. I can answer this without making any changes - it's purely informational.\n\nThe DLL search order on Windows (simplified):\n1. The directory where the executable (Main.exe) is located\n2. The current working directory (this is configurable via `SetDllDirectory` and was removed from default search in modern Windows)\n3. The System32 directory\n4. The directories listed in the %PATH% environment variable\n5. Known DLLs (like kernel32.dll, user32.dll)\n\nSo yes, Main.exe will look for the DLL in its own directory first (by default on modern Windows with Safe DLL Search Mode enabled), and then in PATH.\n\nLet me give a straightforward answer.",
