          "text": "The user is asking for validation of their proposed directory structure. Let me think about what they're suggesting:\n\n\"build в корне out-ы + err, и поддиректории для объектников каждой задачи + common\"\n\nSo the structure would be:\n\n```\nbuild/\n  main_out.txt\n  err.txt\n  common/\n    geometry_c.obj\n    geometry_cpp.obj\n    string_utils_c.obj\n    string_utils_cpp.obj\n    lib_c.lib\n    lib_cpp.lib\n    common_c.dll\n    common_cpp.dll\n  t1_dist_matrix_c/\n    main_c.obj\n    ref_c.obj\n    main_c.exe\n  t1_dist_matrix/\n    main_cpp.obj\n    ref_cpp.obj\n    main_cpp.exe\n  t2_passport_c/\n    ...\n  t2_passport_cpp/\n    ...\n  t3_bbox_c/\n    ...\n  t3_bbox_cpp/\n    ...\n  t4_filter_c/\n    ...\n  t4_filter_cpp/\n    ...\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `main_out.txt` and `err.txt` stay flat in `build/` root (shared, rewritten each run)\n- `.obj`, `.lib`, `.exe`, `.dll` get their own subdirectories per task\n\nThis is reasonable. The test output files (`main_out.txt`, `err.txt`) are temporary and get overwritten each test run, so they can stay flat. The build artifacts need separation.\n\nLet me think about potential issues:\n\n1. **test output files overwriting** — if `make test` runs all tests sequentially, the last one's output stays. The user seems aware of this and it's a minor issue — tests check output and exit code immediately after each run, so the file is consumed before the next test overwrites it. The problem only appears if you examine the file after the full run. But in the make world, tests typically check their own output within the recipe and don't rely on the file persisting.\n\n2. **Clean** — `rm -rf build/` still works\n\n3. **Parallel tests** — if make runs tests in parallel with -j, `main_out.txt` will be corrupted. But the user may not plan to parallelize test execution (only compilation). Even so, it's worth noting.\n\nActually, looking at the current .bat files, each test case does: `prog.exe > build\\main_out.txt` then immediately checks the file with `findstr`. The file is consumed right after it's written, before the next test overwrites it. So from a practical standpoint, the flat `main_out.txt` works fine even within a single task's test suite.\n\nThe structure she's proposing is clean and pragmatic. I should validate and note the single risk (parallel test execution), but otherwise approve.",
